This project is original code. It does not vendor third-party source, but it is
designed to interoperate with / was informed by the following open-source work:

Runtime dependencies (installed via pip, their own licenses apply):
  requests              Apache-2.0
  beautifulsoup4        MIT
  websockets            BSD-3-Clause
  PyYAML                MIT
  python-dotenv         BSD-3-Clause
  pytest (dev only)     MIT

Data sources / services:
  aisstream.io                       free real-time AIS WebSocket API
  Open-Meteo                          marine + weather forecast API (CC-BY 4.0)
  AFAD deprem.afad.gov.tr             public earthquake event API
  USGS earthquake.usgs.gov           earthquake GeoJSON feed (US Gov, public domain)
  EMSC seismicportal.eu              earthquake FDSN event service
  Sahil Güvenlik Komutanlığı          official announcements
  GDACS (gdacs.org)                   global disaster alerts RSS
  NASA EONET (eonet.gsfc.nasa.gov)   natural event tracking API (US Gov)
  ReliefWeb (api.reliefweb.int)      OCHA humanitarian data API
  aviationweather.gov (NOAA/AWC)      METAR API (US Gov, public domain)
  NGA MSI (msi.nga.mil)              NAVAREA navigational warnings (US Gov)
  AA / Hürriyet / NTV / Sözcü / CNN Türk / TRT / Habertürk / Milliyet /
    Denizhaber / gCaptain             news RSS (headlines, keyword filtered)
  OpenStreetMap / OpenSeaMap          map tiles (ODbL)
  Leaflet 1.9.4 (CDN)                BSD-2-Clause

Referenced by src/sdr/ (integration guides only — not bundled):
